# tools/test_media.sha256 — every file of the test-media archive
# (archive.org item pom68k_media, pom68k_media.zip): SHA-256 and repository
# path, `sha256sum -c` format. tools/fetch_test_media.py installs each file
# the tree lacks, after checking it against this list; tools/build_asset_archives.py
# media builds the zip from a tree that has them.
#
# The list is explicit on purpose: hdv/ on the reference host is 6.2 GB of
# work copies, PRAM files and scratch volumes, and none of that belongs in
# the archive. Two groups, 914.5 MiB uncompressed in all:
#  1. every reference-disk / reference-floppy row of assets.lock (the
#     etalons' qualified media, read-only under hdv/ref and disks35/ref);
#  2. the other images asset-requiring gates open by name and the
#     reference host holds (System 6.0.8 / 5.1 volumes for
#     compact_teachtext_etalon, compact_savestate_relaunch_etalon and
#     scsi_hfs_facade_test; the floppies of se_three_drive_etalon).
# Images gates name that the reference host does not hold — hdv/boot.vhd
# (1.4 GB, a last-resort fallback), hdv/MacOS-7.6-boot.vhd, the CD images
# (MAC_OS_8-1_RETAIL_0.ISO, MacOS_86.iso, Apeiron_1_0_3.toast,
# GliderPRO_1_1_2.toast, TIM_3.iso), disks35/Disk605.moof,
# disks35/Oids v1.4.moof and disks35/Stuffit_Expander_5.5.dsk — are not
# listed; their gates soft-skip without them, as they do today.

